  "final_span": "are trying to make learning fun and give them a visual which helps them remember their new found knowledge.\u201d It's uncertain whether the students enjoy Mr. Swanson's hip-hop style enough to seek out artists like Kendrick Lamar, but they clearly relish listening to their teacher rap.\nMr. Swanson features other notable artists from his K-12, Syracuse, and North Syracuse student roster, including \"Gucci Thizz\" (sic), according to Swanson, who is notably inspired by \"Stop Snitching\" by East Coast rap groups Yall So Cold. Even if Gucci's SoundCloud was linked, it wouldn't have been noticed by us unless his crude username didn't interfere completely, as its presence would not clearly indicate a leading profile for listeners over fifteen years old. It's entirely possible that Mr Swanson\u2019s kidnap-themed track is much more innocent than we suspect, but would the children at North Syracuse High truly appreciate the refined skill in delivery if it weren't related to themes distant from Britney Spears\u2019 \u201cSwitch,\u201d leading to improvements rather than problematic outcomes for the foreseeable future? More loaded Swanson explorations, all set to beefy club remixes, are expected on \u201choliday\u201d soon as Swanson is in \u201cserious discussions\u201d with a producer about \u201cturning my teacher raps into big room bangers for the older students.\u201d Most currently, and perhaps unrelatedly, he has released, and is trying to sell, their \u201cNear Film Character\u201d \u2014 a gimcrack, Hasbro/Playmobil-style \u201cstep brother character that has to be glued together to work properly.\u201d The \u201cfun and tasteless violation scene,\u201d according to a listing on the website for Mr Swanson\u2019s FingerLakesGoods shop, is available in both \u201cgory and damaged sets.\u201d Two pictures available for review appear to include a head detached from its body.\nPresent Swanson adjectives, harshly assessed or not, would by definition include inspiring, motivating, and relatable and are \u201cexpected to be able to go beyond the classroom,\u201d and level teachers and classrooms any",
